      "status": "ok",
      "output": {
        "decision": "answer",
        "reason": "The evidence identifies two shortcomings (overconfidence in predictions and incomplete transcripts when language models are used) and provides partial solutions: efficient regularization/careful decoding in the conclusions, and for partial transcripts three strategies — forbidding EOS unless within a set probability range of the most probable token, extending beam search with a length-promoting term, and a coverage term counting frames with cumulative attention above a threshold to prevent looping. The evidence does not give full detail on the overconfidence solution (regularization is only referenced at a high level), but the main proposed solutions are described."
      },
      "elapsed_ms": 2735.2426999714226
    },
